# Exclusions for the D3DMetal backend (Neptune: Windows arm64 guest + viogpu3d/Triton over
# the host's D3DMetal):
#   dxcts run --per-group --backend d3dmetal --exclusion d3dmetal
# One flat JSON object per line; "reason" is required.  See docs/exclusions.md.
{"binary":"WGF11SharedResources.exe","reason":"Exhausts host GPU memory, a host-panic risk: cross-process shared-resource groups leave D3DMetal allocations behind until Metal aborts command buffers with Insufficient Memory (kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorOutOfMemory).  A host kernel panic (2026-09-04, WindowServer watchdog) followed exactly that storm; on 2026-10-17 it recurred 3,181 s into the binary, in ShareFromDX11\\ToGDI after ShareFromDX11\\ToDX11/ToDX10_1/ToDX10_0 had taken 833/637/1,469 s, and only the host's GPU-fault watchdog stopping the VM kept the host up.  The memory builds up across groups, so no single group can be named; finding one would mean deliberately re-running a host-fault reproducer.","evidence":"WGF11SharedResources in the Neptune full sweep of 2026-10-15 (the watchdog's and QEMU's logs); the traces of the 2026-09-04 host panic"}
{"binary":"MemChecker.exe","reason":"Allocates until video memory runs out, and on this backend that is host GPU memory: on 2026-10-17 the render worker then spun at 100% CPU for 22 min inside D3DMetal D3DMCommandEncoder::FlushClears on one ring command while the guest waited on ring 1, until the VM was killed.  D3D9 runs through D3D9On12's own D3D12 device, which the d3dmetal layer does not wrap, so there is nothing for the harness to bound.","evidence":"MemChecker in the Neptune full sweep of 2026-10-15: a sample of the spinning render worker, and the guest's partial output"}
{"binary":"D3DConf_12_Core.dll","group":"D3DConf_12_0_ResourceBinding","reason":"Hangs the host GPU, a host-panic risk: three times in three runs of this class, 2026-10-18 23:52, 2026-10-20 04:05 and 07:20, Metal aborted a command buffer with kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorHang (or discarded it as a victim of the recovery) and the host's GPU-fault watchdog stopped the VM.  An entry for MaxDescriptorHeapSizeSM51Test alone, where the guest output of the second run last stood, did not prevent the third: it hung inside the class again, at the same point of the host log as before -- 64 KiB heap imports from guest shared memory, 11,455 against 11,463 and 11,465, the HeapTests storm (4,226 a minute) and then this class's.  So the trigger is not that test, the output cannot name the one that is (TAEF writes it in arrears and the last snapshot predates the hang), and narrowing it further would mean deliberately re-running a host GPU hang.","evidence":"D3DConf_12_Core in the Neptune D3DMetal sweep of 2026-10-18 to 2026-10-20: the run with the SM51-only entry and the GPU-hang run (QEMU and watchdog logs, the guest's partial output); the 2026-10-18 heap-import profile from the host log; the rerun with this entry, in which the binary runs to the end"}
{"binary":"D3DConf_12_Video.dll","group":"Conf_VideoNative","reason":"Kills the VM, through a QEMU fault rather than the test: QEMU aborts on `Assertion failed: (isv), function hvf_vcpu_exec, file hvf.c, line 2295` (a guest data abort it cannot emulate), and the runner and every later group go with it.  Three times out of three runs on this backend -- 2026-10-16, 2026-10-17 and 2026-10-20, each about 76 min into this class -- and at different cases (the per-case output last reached SimpleGOPEncodeHEVC data sets 422 and 207), so the trigger builds up inside the class and no narrower selection would hold.  The same assert has also ended WGF11SharedResources and 10L9Blend runs, so it is QEMU's, and the entry goes when QEMU is fixed.  The class runs to completion elsewhere (14,585 cases in 809 s on CrossOver).","evidence":"D3DConf_12_Video in the Neptune D3DMetal sweep of 2026-10-18 (QEMU log, the guest's partial output) and in the Neptune full sweep of 2026-10-15, with QEMU's own crash reports"}
{"binary":"D3DConf_12_Core.dll","group":"D3DConf_12_0_DebugLayerScenarios","cases":"NonResourceStateValidation*","reason":"Exhausts host GPU memory, a host-panic risk: on 2026-10-20 09:39, inside this method, Metal aborted command buffers with Insufficient Memory (kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorOutOfMemory) and the host's GPU-fault watchdog stopped the VM.  Before that, its rows kill the render worker one after another (seven times in that run, nine in the 08:14 run): libmetalirconverter SIGSEGV in LazyLinker::CollectReferencedSymbols under DXIL2AIR::assemble, a D3DMetal shader-converter defect.  The guest survives each death, but the run cannot get through the method: the output stands at its first data set's last row in both runs, and the rows after that (metadataSet1-7) are where the memory ran out, which only re-running a host GPU fault could narrow.  All 64 rows; TE /list over the class gives 607 rows without this entry and 543 with it, the 64 named.  The other 543 rows of the class run.","evidence":"D3DConf_12_Core in the Neptune D3DMetal sweep: the out-of-memory run of 2026-10-20 09:39 (watchdog and QEMU logs, the guest's partial output) and the 08:14 run with the nine render-worker segfaults and their crash reports"}
